  </data>
  <data name="ActionQuery_TOOLTIP" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use Action Query to execute an procedure and return a single value.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExecuteQuery_DESCRIPTION" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The ExecuteQuery functoid is used for executing queries from the database. Each query will only be executed once. The functoid requires the following input parameters in this order: (1)the connection string or the key reference to the config file, (2) a flag "true" or "false" telling the functoid to search cache or not, (3) the name of the source that is providing the data (table or stored procedure). The following is optional: [a column name, lookup value] or [sp parameter, parameter value].  The functoid can take a maximum of 6 pairs of either [column name and value] or [sp parameter, parameter value].</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExecuteQuery_ICON" type="System.Resources.ResXFileRef, System.Windows.Forms">
    <value>..\resources\executequery_icon.bmp;System.Drawing.Bitmap, System.Drawing, Version=2.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b03f5f7f11d50a3a</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExecuteQuery_NAME" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Execute Query</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExecuteQuery_TOOLTIP" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The Execute Query functoid is used for executing queries to a database table. </value>
  </data>
  <data name="ExtractData_DESCRIPTION" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use the Value Extractor functoid to extract the appropriate column value from a recordset returned by the Execute Query functoid. This functoid requires two input parameters: a link to the ExecuteQuery functoid and a column name. It takes an optional extra 6 pairs of parameters [column name and value]. When the optional parameters are used the Execute Query functoid is forced to have the whole table cached.</value>
  </data>
